# OksaSDR tour, "On the air": 80 m SSB in the evening, tuned onto stations: each station's
# voice band found in a 10 kHz view and the dial on its carrier (LSB: the band's sharp top
# edge at the dial), checked from the picture before use (the user: the passband on the
# station, never between two). 2.9 kHz receive filter. 3.663 (-85 dBm) and 3.778 (spare).
pin 5
record 15
caption !speed 3
caption # On the air
caption Each mode as it sounds on the band right now, live from the radio.
ready
wait 4000
caption !speed 1
caption SSB on 80 m in the evening: tap the frequency and type it.
caption !mark 240,145
frequency-dialog
wait 1500
keys 3.663
wait 1500
keys <Enter>
wait 1500
span 10
wait 2000
caption Then the mode: LSB, the sideband of the low bands.
caption !mark 560,115
mode LSB
wait 2500
caption Phone sounds fuller with the 2.9 kHz receive filter: tap the filter width, then 2.9k.
caption !mark 933,115
popup filterChooser
wait 2000
taptext 2.9k
wait 2000
close
wait 1000
caption @ssb 3.663
caption 80 m SSB at 3.663 MHz: the station's voice fills the passband, LSB with the 2.9 kHz filter.
wait 45000
caption @ssb 3.778
caption 80 m SSB at 3.778 MHz: the station's voice fills the passband, LSB with the 2.9 kHz filter.
freq 3.778
span 10
wait 30000
caption @ssb end
caption -
record off
freq 14.074
mode DIGU
wait 2000
slices
